#>wonder_state_block_projections_lens_seat
?["Which lens seat should the site wear: A, the authored chassis; B, a seat row that shows its own expression; or C, a silent row?"]{
  #:depth #!experiential ~#lens(choice)
  ~#with: @plan
  ~#hypothesis: "One review at /design/components/#lens-seats settles four gates. They are the seat treatment, the faint inactive mode-switch chips (from attention-shell-contrast), the lens-use reward toast that reads the seat expression (from mindful-collection-controls), and when a sat seat is offered to the cauldron (cauldron-lens-composition). On a phone the seats measure about 170px (A), 121px (B) and 100px (C)."
  ~#tension: "B teaches the notation: the seat a reader presses is the token that changes in about[kernel]{open.sit}. C is the quietest and spends the least height. A keeps the feedback line and state dot that some readers may lean on. The pick is a feel decision, so it is made in a browser and not by measurement."
  ~#expect: "Until the look, the rg half shows the seat value only under page_design_components in design.css (:1686) and only silent and quiet in state-semantics.css; after a B or C pick, a seat rule sits in state-semantics.css Cluster C."
  ~#unblocks: "PLAN.md slices 1 and 2: the seat promotion and the lens reward"
  ~#probe(read)
  !probe{ "Open /design/components/#lens-seats on a phone and a desktop, press each seat in A, B and C, and pick one; then rg -n 'lens-chrome' public/css/routes/surfaces/design.css public/css/handles/operators/state-semantics.css" }
  $%[seat.chassis, seat.row, seat.silent]
  ~<"./PLAN.md"> ~<"../../../design/components/index.html">
}

#>wonder_state_block_projections_first_token
?["Which token should be the first one a reader can press in a state block?"]{
  #:depth #!semantic ~#lens(choice)
  ~#with: @plan @lens_modes
  ~#taste: "A state block earns its notation when pressing a token changes the thing the token names, and the reader watches it change."
  ~#hypothesis: "The lens [mode] token is the right first one: its owner, lens-modes.js, already takes requests from five callers, so a pressable token adds an asker and no writer, and row B already shows the expression it would rewrite."
  ~#tension: "The satchel's page line reaches every page but is floating chrome at the compact pocket target; the image effect cycle (semantic, pixelize, watercolor, clarify) already has helper chips, so a token there repeats a control."
  ~#expect: "rg finds requestLensMode( in five callers and the seat expression written only in lens-modes.js; nothing renders a pressable token yet."
  ~#unblocks: "PLAN.md slice 4, the expression-is-the-switch bench demo, and whether slice 3 retires the disclosure event or hands it to the token"
  ~#probe(run)
  !probe{ "rg -n 'requestLensMode\\(' public/js" }
  $%[token.lens_mode, token.satchel_page_line, token.image_effect]
}

#>wonder_state_block_projections_seat_projection
?["Should a seat line's <projection> stay the seat's authored first room, or follow the reader to the next room in that seat they have not opened yet?"]{
  #:depth #!experiential ~#lens(choice)
  ~#with: @plan @wip
  ~#hypothesis: "Perusing reads better when the line points where this reader has not been: the braces already hold what they carried here from other pages, so the angle brackets could hold where to go next, shown before the step is taken."
  ~#tension: "The site keeps no record of rooms opened by path (the component collection stores surface names; visited image surfaces keep their pages), so following the reader needs a reading the site does not have yet, and no new store may be added without review; the authored first move is honest and stable."
  ~#expect: "No store records rooms opened by path: component-collection.js keeps surface names, and kernel/visited-surfaces-storage.js keeps pages only for image surfaces a reader marked visited."
  ~#unblocks: "a perusing mechanic on Home that carries across pages, and whether the seat line can become the switch (slice 4)"
  ~#probe(read)
  !probe{ "rg -n 'routes.push|visited' public/js/runtime/memory/component-collection.js public/js/kernel/visited-surfaces-storage.js" }
  $%[projection.authored, projection.next_unopened, projection.both_named]
}
